---
import sharedCss from '../../public/styles/shared.css?raw';
// ⚠ ?raw + set:html, NOT an Astro style-tag import. This block MUST stay is:inline:
// (that sentence deliberately avoids writing the literal tag — a bare mention of it
//  in a comment is what made an earlier parser swallow 7KB of frontmatter as CSS)
// `is:global` was tried and shipped the homepage with 0 bytes inline plus a
// render-blocking <link> — measured, on the landing page. `?raw` keeps assembly
// ours, so the CSS is inlined verbatim and still has ONE source (shared.css).
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The AICV homepage. Converted from public/index.html to an Astro page on
// 2026-08-09 (Phase 2) for ONE reason: the recent-articles section needs the
// news collection, and a static file in public/ cannot read it at build time.
//
// The OTHER FIVE PAGES REMAIN STATIC HTML IN public/. That asymmetry is
// deliberate — only this page needs the collection. Do not "fix" it by
// converting the rest; that is a separate decision with its own verification.
//
// The alternatives were rejected: a prebuild script rewriting public/index.html
// mutates a tracked source file on every build; injecting into dist/ makes the
// deployed homepage stop being the file you edit; and a client-side fetch is
// invisible to agents, which is why the D3 graph was removed in 2e3dce8.
//
// ⚠ THE STYLE BLOCK BELOW MUST KEEP `is:inline`. Two failure modes, both real,
// both caught in Stage 2 verification on 2026-08-09:
//
//   · plain style      -> Astro SCOPES it. Every rule stops matching this
//                         hand-written markup and the page renders unstyled.
//   · style is:global  -> not scoped, but Astro EXTRACTS the CSS to
//                         /_astro/*.css. Verified: the page shipped with zero
//                         inline CSS and a render-blocking stylesheet link,
//                         while the other five pages keep 15-24KB inline. That
//                         adds a round trip before first paint on the landing
//                         page, and silently diverges it from the rest of the
//                         site.
//
// `is:inline` opts out of ALL Astro processing: the CSS ships exactly as
// authored, in place, matching the other five pages.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import eventsData from '../data/events.json';

// DERIVED, not typed. The homepage and /events must state the SAME number, and
// the only way to guarantee that is to read the same file.
//
// This markup is ordinary Astro and interpolates, so the visible prose derives
// properly. The JSON-LD below CANNOT — it is `is:inline` — so the count there
// stays a written constant with a build assertion in scripts/prepare-feeds.mjs
// holding it to this same file. That asymmetry is the whole reason the assertion
// exists; see the 2026-08-11 events entry in STATE.md.
const sessionCount = eventsData.events.length;

const articles = (await getCollection('news'))
  .filter((a) => !a.data.draft)
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.getTime() - a.data.date.getTime())
  .slice(0, 3);

const fmt = (d) =>
  d.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
