<!-- ── WHY NOW ── -->
<section class="section section--dark section--sm" id="why-now">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--dim">Why Now</span>
    <h2 class="h2 h2--lt">The AI revolution is no longer a future prediction</h2>
    <p class="body body--lt body--lead">It is actively reshaping the Coachella Valley's economy today by rapidly changing local job requirements and business models. As the region's dedicated boots-on-the-ground, AICV is uniquely positioned to ensure this transformation fuels local growth rather than widening our economic divide. By scaling targeted training and small business tech integration right now, we can turn this massive technological shift into an unprecedented era of sustainable desert prosperity.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── PROGRAMS ── -->
<section class="section section--sand" id="programs">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Programs</span>
    <h2 class="h2">What we're building.</h2>
    <div class="programs-intro">
      <p class="body">AICV's programs are designed to turn AI literacy into applied skills and real opportunity across the Coachella Valley.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ⚠ THE CARDS ARE EVERGREEN — RULED 2026-08-26. A program card is a
         PERMANENT surface: it is read months after it is written, by people who
         have no way to know when it was written. A dated claim on one goes stale
         silently, with no gate to catch it.

         So a claim here either DERIVES from data or it does not belong on a card.
         Two were replaced on this ruling: "Bilingual sessions begin in September"
         (card 1) and "Open now; first demo night this fall" (card 2). Both had
         already outlived the sentence that made them true. Announcements with a
         date belong in a news post, which is stamped and sorted and reads as of
         its moment.

         The count in card 1 is {sessionCount} for the same reason — it derives
         from src/data/events.json rather than being typed. Do not re-type it. -->
    <div class="prog-grid">

      <div class="prog-card prog-card--featured" aria-label="Live program">
        <span class="prog-pill pill-live">Live</span>
        <div class="prog-num">1</div>
        <h3 class="prog-title">AICV Workshops</h3>
        <p class="prog-tagline">Hands-on AI training at CSUSB Palm Desert.</p>
        <p class="prog-body">{sessionCount} sessions across six series for small business owners, students, nonprofit staff, and people whose jobs are changing. Sessions in English and Spanish.</p>
        <a href="/events" class="prog-tag">See upcoming sessions →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="prog-card prog-card--featured" aria-label="Live program">
        <span class="prog-pill pill-live">Live</span>
        <div class="prog-num">2</div>
        <h3 class="prog-title">AI Tinkerers Coachella Valley</h3>
        <p class="prog-tagline">Demos, not decks. Builders, not spectators.</p>
        <p class="prog-body">The valley's chapter of the world's largest hands-on AI builders' community — screened, demo-first, no pitches. It gathers the region's strongest AI builders into one room: the talent that mentors the next generation and trains the trainers. Demo nights, build days, and a global hackathon.</p>
        <a href="https://coachella-valley.aitinkerers.org" class="prog-tag" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join the chapter →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="prog-card prog-card--featured" aria-label="Live program">
        <span class="prog-pill pill-live">Live</span>
        <div class="prog-num">3</div>
        <h3 class="prog-title">The AI Beat</h3>
        <p class="prog-tagline">Reporting AI across the Inland Empire.</p>
        <p class="prog-body">The Coachella Valley sits inside the Inland Empire, and almost no one is covering how AI is actually landing here — in classrooms, city halls, clinics, and small businesses. Sat Singh reports the AI beat at Informed IE, with original reporting from AICV. Funded by the <a href="https://iejournalism.fund/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IE Journalism Innovation Hub+Fund</a>, the Press Forward Inland Empire chapter.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

